# f2 = watch. The program of a-guard-that-a-read-leans-on-is-asked-again-in-the-turn-under-its-own-word.ir.
# A read of a slot that may be empty skips the lookup on the prototype chain where the walk's state remembers that the class guard holds.
# That guard is tested again before the read, and the process ends if it does not hold.
# This happens with testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime, and also with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, which --aot-harden=proof-checks enables.
# The reason is that a guard that had been invalidated unnoticed is how a silent miscompilation got past the proof checks.
# With the two fixes of that miscompilation reverted, six of its ten programs silently print wrong results with the option, and crash with a named error once the guard is tested again.
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Operation/PutSlotOrAdd/MemberGuards: the effects entry of PutSlotOrAdd falsely claims that the operation invalidates no guard.
# The second version of the loop tests the guard once, in the preheader, and its iteration relies on that. The test that is built again is in the iteration.
# RUN(OPTION): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Operation/PutSlotOrAdd/MemberGuards,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# OPTION: isLoopHead=true
# OPTION: isLoopHead=true
# OPTION: [[again]]: boolean @Boolean = AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{layout=L0 key="note"}]
# OPTION-NEXT: CheckProof [[again]] checkedType=true {{*}}source=RememberedFact
# OPTION: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}} key="note"
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 0 14 20 above tag
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RIGHT-NEXT: the source prints the same
